From: packaging
Subject: [PATCH] link EGL without a GLVND OpenGL::EGL target

CMake's FindOpenGL only creates the OpenGL::EGL imported target when
GLVND is present. Chimera builds Mesa with -Dglvnd=disabled, so
libEGL exists (and OPENGL_egl_LIBRARY is set) but the target is not.
The existing NetBSD/OpenBSD branch already links the raw library.

https://codeberg.org/letoram/arcan/commit/76d6603e547386117e43aaa2737824a6dd9999eb

---
 src/platform/cmake/CMakeLists.Video | 4 ++--
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/platform/cmake/CMakeLists.Video b/src/platform/cmake/CMakeLists.Video
--- a/src/platform/cmake/CMakeLists.Video
+++ b/src/platform/cmake/CMakeLists.Video
@@ -54,7 +54,7 @@ elseif(VIDEO_PLATFORM STREQUAL "egl-dri")
 
 # workaround CMake FindOpenGL module messing up because GLVND
 # on non-linux systems.
-	if (${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} MATCHES "NetBSD|OpenBSD")
+	if (${CMAKE_SYSTEM_NAME} MATCHES "NetBSD|OpenBSD" OR NOT TARGET OpenGL::EGL)
 		list(APPEND VIDEO_LIBRARIES
 			${OPENGL_egl_LIBRARY}
 			${GBMKMS_LINK_LIBRARIES}
